# Playwright per-run output. The HTML report and traces are debugging
# artifacts for one run against a throwaway fixture — never source.
#
# GLOB, NOT AN EXACT NAME. `playwright-report/` matched the smoke suite's output
# and NOTHING ELSE — a trailing-slash pattern is a literal directory name, so it
# never covered the canary's `playwright-report-canary/`. That gap put four real
# trace archives into a commit, and a Playwright trace records full request and
# response bodies: 36 plaintext occurrences of the sim Owner's password, 60 JWTs
# and 24 refresh-cookie entries went in as plaintext inside a zip, which
# GitGuardian's scan did not see.
#
# The HTML report is credential-bearing BY CONSTRUCTION, not only when a trace
# rides along: Playwright embeds a base64 copy of the run inside `index.html` and
# renders step titles containing literal fill values, so a sign-in step reads
# `Fill "<the password>"`. There is no variant of these directories that is safe
# to commit.
#
# So: match the family, and treat any new Playwright output directory as covered
# by default rather than by remembering to add it.
test-results*/
playwright-report*/
blob-report*/
.last-run.json

# Screenshots/videos the canary (#386) writes outside the report dir.
artifacts/
